WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.490
- So, last time you were here,

00:00:01.490 --> 00:00:02.323
I thought you said you were like,

00:00:02.323 --> 00:00:03.156
"No, I'm done with Madea"

00:00:03.156 --> 00:00:03.989
and I love that you brought her back.

00:00:03.989 --> 00:00:05.020
I feel like we need her.

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:06.050
She makes me laugh.

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:06.883
(audience cheers)

00:00:06.883 --> 00:00:07.716
- I tell you.

00:00:07.716 --> 00:00:09.367
- She makes me so happy.

00:00:09.367 --> 00:00:10.700
- I tell you what happened.

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:12.110
And that's exactly why I brought her back.

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:13.040
Looking at the pandemic,

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:15.330
looking at all the
social and civil unrest,

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:16.360
looking at all the madness

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:17.890
and looking at everything
that's happened in the country.

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:19.040
I'm like, "We need to laugh."

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:20.450
All of our smiles were covered up.

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:21.950
I'm like, "What do I have in my toolbox

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:23.170
that will make people laugh?"

00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:25.110
And I open it up and
somebody says, "Hello."

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:25.943
- (Kelly) Hello!

00:00:25.943 --> 00:00:28.031
- And here we are, so yeah, on Netflix,

00:00:28.031 --> 00:00:28.864
I'm excited.

00:00:28.864 --> 00:00:29.697
- I love it!

00:00:29.697 --> 00:00:30.750
I know it makes me so happy,

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:32.440
and I love, this was a specific,

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:36.370
it's, you spoke about LGBTQ
community in this one.

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:37.203
I think it's cool.

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:38.036
It's a different message.

00:00:38.036 --> 00:00:38.869
- (Tyler) Yeah.

00:00:38.869 --> 00:00:40.130
- For this Madea, was that
really important to you?

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:42.260
- Yeah, I just, again
looking at the trauma

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:44.770
and the heartache and how
much everybody has to say

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:46.940
about other people and the
way they live their lives.

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:48.439
You get one life, life is short, right?

00:00:48.439 --> 00:00:50.410
So I wanted to show a gay character

00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:52.171
coming out to his family, a Black family.

00:00:52.171 --> 00:00:53.004
- (Kelly) Yeah.

00:00:53.004 --> 00:00:54.810
- And they're embracing
him and showing him love.

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:56.210
- I was just gonna say, I loved that.

00:00:56.210 --> 00:00:57.330
I loved that it actually did that.

00:00:57.330 --> 00:00:58.163
- It's a great example.

00:00:58.163 --> 00:00:59.990
- It wasn't like the
typical, like, oh, it's hard.

00:00:59.990 --> 00:01:02.000
'Cause yes, it is hard, you know,

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:03.530
for people, I have friends
that it was hard for-

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:04.820
- (Tyler) Very hard for some, yeah.

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:05.680
- And some of their
family don't talk to them,

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:07.560
but some are, they embrace it.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:08.393
They love you.

00:01:08.393 --> 00:01:09.226
It's not a big deal.

00:01:09.226 --> 00:01:10.530
And I think we don't hear
those stories enough.

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:12.280
- That's why it was so
important for me to show.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:14.220
'Cause I do a lot of
work with Covenant House

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:16.150
who've over the years,
they have, you know,

00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:17.660
a lot of kids are homeless

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:20.220
because they were put out
because they were LGBTQ plus.

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:21.290
And to see-

00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:23.090
- Can you imagine that?

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:23.923
I mean we're both parents.

00:01:23.923 --> 00:01:24.756
- It's horrible.

00:01:24.756 --> 00:01:25.589
- What?

00:01:25.589 --> 00:01:26.422
- I don't even know how.

00:01:26.422 --> 00:01:27.255
Listen, I couldn't even imagine,

00:01:27.255 --> 00:01:29.500
the love that I have for my child.

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:30.333
- (Kelly) Infinite.

00:01:30.333 --> 00:01:31.630
- Infinite, you know?

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:34.330
And to think because of
the way they were born

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:35.696
you would really just discard them,

00:01:35.696 --> 00:01:37.431
is shocking to me that people can do that.

00:01:37.431 --> 00:01:38.264
- (Kelly) Yeah.

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:39.097
- Yeah.

00:01:39.097 --> 00:01:39.930
- I don't get that either.

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:40.763
- Yeah.

00:01:40.763 --> 00:01:42.310
- I think it's really cool
that you use a powerful message

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:45.010
in such a powerful way
because people love to laugh.

00:01:45.010 --> 00:01:47.190
They love to, they're already
a part of this character,

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:48.023
they love the-

00:01:48.023 --> 00:01:48.856
- Thank you babe, I appreciate.

00:01:48.856 --> 00:01:49.890
I appreciate it so much.

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:50.747
I appreciate so much, I appreciate babe.

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:54.010
I've been around a long time.

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:56.160
